{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14279-how-cover-developed","id":14279,"title":"How Cover developed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-19T14:07:58-08:00","id":14279,"title":"How Cover developed","content":"I originally posted on th<span style=\"color:#0B1902\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">e KS page, but thought it might be interesting to talk about it here, as well.<br /> <br /> (A lot more details on the mechanics are available in the full-text preview. If you haven't checked it out, it's on the <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\">&lt;project page on Kickstarter&gt;</a>.)<br /> <br /> One of my favorite aspects of Demon is Cover, and I\u2019d like to talk a little bit about how we developed it. Cover is your character\u2019s false life, the lie they tell both to the people in their lives and to reality itself.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0B1902\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The idea of the double (or triple) life is a compelling one, because it leads right back to questions we all ask ourselves. Who am I, really? Am I actually the person the people who love me see? These are great questions to ask about our characters in games, too -- and in a game, we might get more definitive answers. <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">(As a side note, I recommend Vonnegut\u2019s <i>Mother Night</i> as a really interesting look at these questions, appropriate to a Demon game in a low key way.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Cover was a fairly early part of the Demon proposal. After years of developing Vampire, and exploring the link between the Masquerade and Humanity, I was interested in a game that essentially conflated the two -- that measured your \u201cintegrity\u201d by how well you pulled off the big lies.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">So it entered the initial bible as a simple concept. Cover was the false life you took with you when you first escaped God. It replaced Integrity (which at this point was still called Morality). It could sometimes be used to resist supernatural effects, as the demon essentially blends too well to be affected by the uncanny.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">As we started to build the mechanics, though, we had to ask some more questions. How do you get Cover back? Can you get a new one? At the same time, we were looking for what demons got out of soul pacts. That\u2019s where the magic started to happen.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">What if, one of the writers asked, you could build your own life out of the pieces of other people\u2019s? Bargain with them for things they might not even want, but which are like diamonds for a fallen angel seeking a place in the world? And then... what if you could just assume another person\u2019s identity entirely?<br /> What if the point wasn\u2019t bargaining for the soul, but for the box it came in? One by one, these questions led to the pact system, a unique way in which demons both exploit and relate to human beings.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">And then, more questions. If I\u2019m so good at pretending to be somebody, why can\u2019t the universe back me up from time to time? Give me a little boost to pretending to be who I need to be? And from there sprang Legend.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I like Cover because it allows us to ask some hard questions about our characters, while at the same time being immensely gameable. You don\u2019t just ask \u201cwho am I and who do I want to be?\u201d; the game mechanics encourage you to engage with it. And that can lead to some really cool emotional moments at the table.</span></span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 11-19-2013, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T14:47:50-08:00","id":14305,"title":"","content":"I admit, Cover is the aspect of the game that seems to appeal most to my players as they've read through the book. Or at least, with myself and a couple others in the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T17:19:14-08:00","id":14387,"title":"","content":"I'll echo the sentiment, honestly how to handle Cover is one of the things I'm most excited about when I think of actually getting to play in a Demon game. I think my concern so far has been how does one balance the treatment of the Cover as a false life with the action/meat of a game session, particularly in Rings where the Demons can have very different Covers?<br /> <br /> Part of me is thinking it's like Hunting in Vampire; something to occasionally engage in as part of a session to remind characters of just <i>who </i>they're pretending to be, while other times maintaining your Cover could be handled by rolls. I'm not sure how I'd do that second part, though.<br /> <br /> I find it such an intensely fascinating mechanic though. Kudos to you guys!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T19:15:21-08:00","id":15051,"title":"","content":"Cover and the mechanical and narrative systems interacting with it are what sell me on Demon, despite being really not sold on the God-Machine itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T20:01:27-08:00","id":15071,"title":"","content":"One of the most low-key and yet poignant events in my Demon playtests had to do with Cover. Two of the characters ended up working very well together and grew somewhat close. Or as close as two characters can get over the course of two or three game sessions.<br /> <br /> Anyway, some events happened in game where they had to investigate a place but didn't want to be seen to do so, so they both switched Covers, and told each other about it. That sharing of &quot;Hey, this is the person I am when I'm not this person you usually know&quot; turned out to be very poignant at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T02:30:40-08:00","id":15267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14279-how-cover-developed?p=15071#post15071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sharing of &quot;Hey, this is the person I am when I'm not this person you usually know&quot; turned out to be very poignant at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of a MtAs game where, before the group went into a scene that stood a good chance of being a suicide mission, we stopped and shared our True Names with each other. Just for that moment of trust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T06:47:25-08:00","id":15340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14279-how-cover-developed?p=15267#post15267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reminds me of a MtAs game where, before the group went into a scene that stood a good chance of being a suicide mission, we stopped and shared our True Names with each other. Just for that moment of trust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, exactly like that. Granted, what my players were going into wasn't a suicide mission, but then they had no idea what exactly they were going into either. They weren't sure of the place was controlled by demons, angels, or other (although they knew something was going on there).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T07:06:35-08:00","id":15345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14279-how-cover-developed?p=15071#post15071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, some events happened in game where they had to investigate a place but didn't want to be seen to do so, so they both switched Covers, and told each other about it. That sharing of &quot;Hey, this is the person I am when I'm not this person you usually know&quot; turned out to be very poignant at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's awesome. I hadn't really thought about it that way before, but arguably revealing secondary covers is about as 'naked' as demons can get to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T08:15:42-08:00","id":15391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14279-how-cover-developed?p=15345#post15345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's awesome. I hadn't really thought about it that way before, but arguably revealing secondary covers is about as 'naked' as demons can get to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was pretty much how it played out, yeah. Given that one of the characters (Anya, for those who read my playtest reports on the Demon blog) had a backstory that involved a mortal who found out what she really was and got the hell out of town because of it, it made her revealing a secondary Cover to another demon a big step in her development.<br /> <br /> Out of all the cool shit that happened in that game - using Embeds, Exploits, demonic form abilities and so on - that seemingly small thing stands out. And I think that's very telling about how human the game can really be in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T15:42:31-08:00","id":17977,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Cover is a really fun part of the game--when they hadnt leaked much else and said the morality stat was called Cover, i wasn't sure.. but it really adds good roleplaying incentive and reigns in demon's activities, while also playing up the amoral liar aspect. Cover took center stage in my mummy crossover. The mummy had finally realized that he was seduced and brainwashed by an angel who was under the false cover of &quot;his wife&quot;. The conflict between the wife he thought he was in love with and the idea that she was lying to him the whole time made for some extremely emotional moments (like when he remembered his wife killing him for remembering in his last life). But the Cover then became more interesting when she fell--as the cover effectively rewrites into reality as &quot;real&quot;, by chosing to fall and be with him, all the lies she had fed him became &quot;true&quot;, and he could enjoy all those memories with her as though she really HAD always been his wife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T22:47:29-08:00","id":23549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This doesn't really make sense, since what the demon is blending in as is a human with no increased resistance to the uncanny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural interference is outside the Machine's modeling, though, so a janitor continuing to be a janitor because the system says it is a janitor and couldn't be, say, a newt? Would seem to make internal sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T00:40:40-08:00","id":23595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons are outside the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>They may be outside the system, but they're using the tools of the system. And if the tools of the system would do something, then they're following that rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T01:26:45-08:00","id":23620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_20785_5-ways-modern-espionage-has-left-james-bond-behind.html/?utm_source=facebook&amp;utm_medium=fanpage&amp;utm_campaign=new+article&amp;wa_ibsrc=fanpage\" target=\"_blank\">Cracked</a>, covers are obsolete in modern espionage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. According to Cracked, I'm not a real person. While googling my name would certainly yield results, none of those results would actually be my instance of that name. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I also think Covers in Demon work a little better than that, anyway, since they actually inject those digital footprints into reality, that all real people apparently have.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/635-slaunyeh","name":"Slaunyeh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T01:40:21-08:00","id":23625,"title":"","content":"I think googling my name only leads to one instance of &quot;Yeah, that's me&quot;, and that's an online program for a play I was in in freaking <i>middle school</i> or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T07:15:13-08:00","id":23742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14279-how-cover-developed?p=23595#post23595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They may be outside the system, but they're using the tools of the system. And if the tools of the system would do something, then they're following that rule.</div> </div> </div> </div> This. The Cover is a construct forcing the Demon to conform to a certain unnatural (for it) configuration. Like The Bug actually being way too big to fit in his 'Edgar suit'. It wouldn't be worth much if any Vlad, Spike, or Harry could poke right through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T07:26:59-08:00","id":27173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rules of the system don't allow it. Cover provides no such protection for the angels Cover was created for in the first place. They always use their Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're also fundamentally immune to any power that would directly cause them to diverge from their mission, require two Arcana in Awakening's system to affect with the sort of magic that Unchained use Cover to buffer against (where such magic currently calls for three dots in each Arcanum being used), condense their Traits down to three other things besides Rank, and are naturally nigh-immortal.<br /> <br /> Also Rank as resistance is rather cold comfort compared to what they're afforded by their <i>actual stats</i>. The average Rank 3 angel has about the same Resistance + Rank pool as a starting Cover 7 Unchained by virtue of sheer higher Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-10-2013, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T09:18:09-08:00","id":27252,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">A Cover isn't exactly an &quot;Edgar suit,&quot; however. It's a layer of &quot;false&quot; reality separating a demon's essential self from the rest of the universe. The higher the Cover rating, the thicker the layer, the more the universe treats the demon as if it's in the state(s) defined by its Cover, and the harder it is to change that state outside of the methods permitted by the demon's Cover[1].</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Angels don't benefit from this in part because their covers are thinner, less &quot;real.&quot; When an angel falls and becomes a demon, its cover gets retroactively burned into reality and becomes more solid[2].</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">--------</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">[1] This assumes there's been a consistent rationale for deciding which abilities are affected by Supernatural Tolerance traits and which aren't. I'm still new to WoD, so I don't know how good the developers have been about this.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">[2] See some of the Demon developer blog posts, and maybe the quickstart. I'm not sure they went into this much in the book, unfortunately.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","user":"gapb","date":".  rephrasing, clarification, spelling/grammar 12-10-2013, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}